  "answer": "This has been reported before. The stack trace you posted matches PowerToys#31226. It is a PowerToys Run crash, raised in WindowChromeWorker when Windows reports that desktop composition (DWM) was turned off. That is the same moment your screens went black. The black screen is a Windows or graphics-driver glitch. PowerToys only reacted to it by crashing. The tickets say the cause varies by machine and is usually outside PowerToys, for example graphics driver problems or memory exhaustion. The fix in #31226 is to update PowerToys to 0.96 or newer, because later versions of PowerToys Run handle this more gracefully. You are on 0.86.0, so update PowerToys. You should also update your GPU drivers and Windows. #32530 is a duplicate report (screen went black for a few seconds, then this error) and was closed in favour of #31226."
 },
